  "visualBrief": "Individual São Paulo Cathedral: twin pale Gothic square towers with tall pointed fields/louvered upper stages, corner shafts/pinnacles, steep green octagonal spires and92m crosses. Deep pointed front timber/glass portals, large geometric circular rose and steep central stone gable; broad entrance stairs. Pale buttressed nave/aisles and gabled transepts, faceted southern apse and pale green copper roof family. Broad ribbed green dome and small actual open lantern/cross at70m. Four existing shared stone/continuous limestone/copper/wood graphs, metric UVs, linear tints and four browser levels. Fine carving/sculptural identity/tracery, interiors and exact urban ground/threshold joins are approximate or excluded.",
